 "reasons": "No gaps are claimed fixed, and none of the changed entries opens a gap or breaks anything that passed. The changes also answer the three carried gaps. g1: sc_fire_walks_with_wind now runs at east and at the reversed west, rules out 'walks one way whatever the wind', and its start asserts the bearing, carries= and a fire-free strip. g2: sc_burn_line_walks now reads the burned share of open plantable ground at each of four day ends, at most half, against a wind-off control that has to cross half. If the control fails to flood, the read is left unmeasured and never passes (burned_share_verdict in src/RimMandrake/Pyrelands/validation.py). g3: the leaf no longer claims 'a fire that lights inside the colony' (tree.json burn_line_walks, sheet.md:15). sc_furnace_giant covers the size part of furnacebeast_warms. sc_furnace, sc_furnace_bed and sc_furnace_hide_bank cover the rest, so the leaf is whole. The exam is current: today's tree input_hash is 2151214485…, the same as the frozen one, and the sheet hash matches. It scored 40/40, and the control Reader missed exactly the wind rejects e5 and c3. Sub-threshold note: the scene text puts the smoulder wait after the wind-off reload. The code runs the relight arm first and turns the wind back on in a finally block, so the read happens on shipping settings. Not a gap."
}